# Sample LSP Completion Request

File: ooda/lsp/examples/completion_request.oot

## Request

```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "textDocument/completion",
  "params": {
    "textDocument": {"uri": "file:///home/user/project/main.oo"},
    "position": {"line": 4, "character": 8},
    "context": {"triggerKind": 2}
  }
}
```

## Expected Response (abbreviated)

```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "result": [
    {"label": "&FsReadCap", "kind": 21, "detail": "File system read capability"},
    {"label": "&FsWriteCap", "kind": 21, "detail": "File system write capability"},
    {"label": "fn", "kind": 14, "detail": "Function keyword"},
    {"label": "let", "kind": 14, "detail": "Let binding keyword"}
  ]
}
```

Completion items are sorted by kind, then alphabetically. The 18 capability tokens, 20 keywords, 8 types, and 23 functions are in the canonical stdlib seed.
